    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. it looks good, but i'm worried it's a little too generic. can you make it sound a bit more personal/warmer? like, maybe acknowledge that the hiring team really liked their energy, but we just need a different fit for the team dynamic right now.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Oh, you're absolutely right, the previous draft felt a bit too stiff, like a standard template sent by a robot with no soul. We need to inject some warmth and personality, perhaps even a little bit of that \"goblin\" energy that makes people feel like they're part of a quirky, chaotic family rather than just a cold corporate machine.\n\nHere is a revised version that acknowledges their specific energy and the team dynamic, while still keeping that professional edge:\n\n**Subject:** A Quick Update Regarding Your Software Engineer Interview\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nFirst off, thank you so much for the fantastic energy you brought to our interview last week! We genuinely enjoyed getting to know you, and your enthusiasm for solving complex problems was infectious. It was a pleasure meeting someone who clearly cares so much about the craft.\n\nHowever, after some serious deliberation by our team, we've decided to move forward with another candidate. It wasn't an easy call, as you were clearly a top contender. The reality is that while your skills are impressive, we've found someone whose current trajectory and team dynamics align slightly better with our immediate needs right now.\n\nPlease don't take this personally; it's simply about the specific fit for our current",
